Package: logitbias
Title: Small-Sample Bias of Logistic Regression Coefficients by Simulation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("fossil", "contributors", email = "fossil@users.noreply.github.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Rebuilds the simulation study of Nemes, Jonasson, Genell and Steineck (2009)
    <doi:10.1186/1471-2288-9-56>: draw repeated samples of increasing size from a finite
    population, fit a logistic regression to each, and estimate the first-order small-sample
    bias b1 of each coefficient by an ordinary least squares fit of the mean estimate on 1/n.
    Also gives the analytic first-order bias of the maximum likelihood estimator (Cordeiro and
    McCullagh 1991; Firth 1993) for a population, and the bias-corrected estimate.
